flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a Chrome extension reaches the Chrome Web Store
    accDescr: Merging the release pull request publishes the release, whose isolated build zips the extension from the signed tag and attests it. The workflow Chrome Web Store asks the store for the state of the item, takes the zip only with its provenance, signs in to Google with the OIDC token of GitHub and no stored secret, uploads it and submits it for review. Google reviews it and publishes it to the users; the daily run delivers a release whose review had to wait and reports a rejection.

    merge["You merge the release pull request"]
    build["`The isolated build zips **extension/** from the signed tag and attests it`"]
    status["`*the state of the store*: no review pending, the store lacks the release`"]
    package["`*the package of the release*: the zip, only with its provenance`"]
    signin["Signed in to Google with the OIDC token of GitHub, no stored secret"]
    store["`*deliver*: upload and submit for review`"]
    review["Google reviews the version"]
    users["The users get the new version"]
    daily["Every day: a review that had to wait, a rejection, a warning"]

    merge --> build --> status --> package --> store --> review --> users
    signin --> status
    signin --> store
    daily --> status

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class merge you
    class build,status,package,signin,store,daily bot
    class review,users done
